e typical behavior: The implementation should compute and return the normalized gain without rounding. I'll do that.\n\nCheck \"stronger counterfactual\" - The description mentions \"weighted losses, the stronger counterfactual\". Actually from the agent description: \"For each call subtract loss with the call from loss without it.\" That's simple. \"Normalize gain by at least one prediction token.\" So prediction_tokens at least 1. \"Require both parseability and normalized gain at or above threshold.\" So inclusive.\n\nThus algorithm: iterate over case['calls'] list, for each call: if call['parseable'] is True and (call['loss_without_call'] - call['loss_with_call']) / call['prediction_tokens'] >= threshold, then accepted=True else False. Append to diagnostics list with call_id, accepted, and normalized_gain (the computed value, regardless of acceptance). For accepted_call_ids, list of call_ids where accepted is True, preserving order.\n\nNote: case is the payload object directly. So case['threshold'], case['calls'].\n\nWe must return a dict with 'accepted_call_ids' and 'diagnostics'.\n\nNeed to raise ValueError for infeasible/invalid case? The candidate_artifact says \"Raise ValueError for an infeasible or structurally invalid case instead of silently repairing it.\" So if missing fields, etc. But we assume the input is valid per schema.\n\nImplementation: define solve(case), compute, return dict. Use Python standard library only.\n\nNow produce the JSON response with key \"implementation\" containing Python source as a JSON string. Escape newlines, backslashes, quotes.\n\nI'll write the code:\n\ndef solve(case):\n    threshold = case['threshold']\n    calls = case['calls']\n    accepted_ids = []\n    diagnostics = []\n    for call in calls:\n        gain = call['loss_without_call'] - call['loss_with_call']\n        norm_gain = gain / call['prediction_tokens']\n        accepted = call['parseable'] and norm_gain >= threshold\n        if accepted:\n            accepted_ids.append(call['call_id'])\n        diagnostics.append({\n            'accepted': accepted,\n            'call_id': call['call_id'],\n            'normalized_gain': norm_gain\n        })\n    return {\n        'accepted_call_ids': accepted_ids,\n        'diagnostics': diagnostics\n    }\n\nThat meets the output schema.\n\nMake sure to not mutate case. We are only reading.\n\nNow produce the answer."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":2164,"completion_tokens":1364,"total_tokens":3528,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":2048},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":1178},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":2048,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":116},"system_fingerprint":"fp_8b330d02d0_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}